# Only what `pnpm install` and `pnpm build` need reaches the build context (see Dockerfile).
#
# Two readers use this file. `docker build` lets `**/x` match at the top too. `az acr run` packs
# the upload with the Azure CLI's own reading of it, where `**/x` needs a folder above x, so every
# rule below that must hold at the top is written twice. Nothing filters on the remote side, and
# the Dockerfile's `COPY . .` copies what arrives (docs/07-self-hosting-azure.md, "Without Docker").

# Dependencies, build output and caches: the image builds its own
node_modules
**/node_modules
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
.tsbuild
**/.tsbuild
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.vite
**/.vite

# Never send secrets to the builder
.env
**/.env
.env.*
**/.env.*
!.env.example
.npmrc
**/.npmrc
.envrc
**/.envrc
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
# The Azure template's working files hold real values or a compiled copy of them (.gitignore).
# infra/.env.azure falls under `**/.env.*`. The rest of infra stays: `az acr run` reads its task
# file from the upload.
infra/*.local.bicepparam
infra/*.parameters.json
infra/main.json

# Version control, CI, editors and local tooling
.git
.github
.claude
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
**/Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
**/Desktop.ini

# Scratch, logs and test artefacts
tmp
**/tmp
*.log
**/*.log
test-results
**/test-results
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
blob-report
**/blob-report
playwright/.cache
**/playwright/.cache

# Docs and the Compose file: not part of the build. The Dockerfile stays in: `az acr run` packs
# only what this file lets through and, unlike `az acr build`, does not add the Dockerfile back.
# The runtime image takes nothing but /out from the build stage, so it never holds a copy.
docs
input.md
compose.yaml
.dockerignore
